  "id": "f5b8b0a3-1c1c-5370-ab8e-1f221b5474dd",
  "slug": "slow-cooker-baby-back-ribs",
  "name": "Slow Cooker Baby Back Ribs",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "Slow cooker ribs cooked in a crockpot until tender, then coated with your favorite barbeque sauce for fall off the bone, lip-smacking ribs every time.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Gather all ingredients."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Season ribs with salt and pepper."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Pour 1/2 cup water into the slow cooker, then add ribs. Scatter onion and garlic over top. Cover and cook on Low for 8 hours or High for 4 hours."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "When the ribs are almost finished, preheat the oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C)."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Transfer ribs from the slow cooker to a baking sheet; discard onion and garlic. Coat ribs with barbeque sauce."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Bake ribs in the preheated oven until sauce caramelizes and sticks to meat, 10 to 15 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Enjoy! No need to fire up the grill or smoker to enjoy finger-licking good barbecue ribs. This slow cooker ribs recipe will quickly become your favorite set-it-and-forget-it meal. The fall-off-the bone meat is a surefire crowd-pleaser. Once the meat is perfectly tender, the sauce gets brown and bubbly thanks to a quick session in the oven. No one will know you didn't spend the whole day tending to these these delicious ribs."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 6,
